# Jones et al. 2025: surface-code QCCD architectures.

ruleset "jones"
title "Surface-code QCCD's rules"
about "A trap does one operation of any kind at a time; a rail and a junction hold one ion at a time; a reorder before a split is a gate swap; operations that the schedule says hold the same component never overlap; every operation lasts what the paper's duration law says; each qubit's gates run in the circuit's order, except that consecutive CNOTs in which it plays the same role may run in any order."

use R0, R1, R2, R3, R6b, R8, R14, R24, R26, R27, R29, R30
param serial_kinds = {"gate2", "gate1", "split", "merge", "swap", "measure", "reset"}
param chain_order = "physical"
